On Mon, 4 Apr 2011, Borek Lupomìský wrote:

>   Well, after playing some Crawl recently, I came to believe that the
> reason NetHack's mid- and late-game are such no brainers is the
> resistances system. Eat shrieker or cave spider and whole class of
> dangerous situations are solved in one fell swoop, get GDSM and many
> powerful magical attacks are no longer any threat, etc.

[snip ways how Crawl resistances are harder to get by]

I think that many roguelike developers agree that Nethack's resistance 
approach (eat once, forget forever) is not ideal. There are other 
interesting solutions than just Crawl's, too:

POWDER grants resistances from eating, but they're temporary. I have never 
played it properly, but this could make for a very interesting gameplay, I 
am sure.

IIUC, UnNethack allows resistance from eating, but it's not binary 
anymore: rather, you'll converge (I am not sure if you converge to 100%, 
though I think the first corpse gives 50%).

Another popular idea is to have innate cold resistance to be incompatible 
with innate fire resistance. (See recent patch thread.)

But in any case, it is worth rethinking the resistances, IMHO.

David

